WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.395
This PostgreSQL preview shows how storage and
validation can work together The

00:00:06.422 --> 00:00:12.227
table requires patient ID and encounter date Triage
level must belong to an approved

00:00:12.253 --> 00:00:18.082
list Temperature uses a teaching range Emergency
visits and total

00:00:18.109 --> 00:00:25.401
charge cannot be negative Run the valid example
first Then

00:00:25.427 --> 00:00:32.451
change emergency visits to negative one or use an
unapproved triage label PostgreSQL

00:00:32.478 --> 00:00:38.085
should reject the invalid row That is an example of
moving a documented validity

00:00:38.112 --> 00:00:39.888
rule into the database itself
